# `block(T)` with well-typed values, prelude functions annotated with
# `block(a)` (`map-values`, `values`, `lookup`), and bare `block` (any
# block) all check without warnings, and produce no deprecation warning.
` { type: "block(number)" }
scores: { alice: 95 bob: 87 }

` { type: "block → [symbol]" }
names(b): b keys

bumped: scores map-values(_ + 10)
total: scores values sum
alice: scores lookup(:alice) + 1
all: names(scores)
